---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import LifecycleNotice from "../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj40.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — Interim-Period Deferred Tax Mechanics" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Why \"Part 2\" — Continuing the Tax Effect Accounting Reform Sequence" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Estimating an Effective Tax Rate for Interim Periods" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Coordination With the Interim Reporting Reform Package" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example — Applying an Estimated Annual Effective Tax Rate at Interim" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="callout info callout--centered">RECENCY NOTE: Issued October 16, 2025 alongside ASBJ Statement No. 37, 38, and 39 — details should be cross-checked against ASBJ's current published materials.</div>

    <div class="toc">
      <a href="#s1">1. Conceptual Framework Linkage</a>
      <a href="#s2">2. Scope — Interim-Period Deferred Tax Mechanics</a>
      <a href="#s3">3. Why "Part 2" — Continuing the Tax Effect Accounting Reform Sequence</a>
      <a href="#s4">4. Estimating an Effective Tax Rate for Interim Periods</a>
      <a href="#s5">5. Coordination With the Interim Reporting Reform Package</a>
      <a href="#s6">6. Worked Example — Applying an Estimated Annual Effective Tax Rate at Interim</a>
      <a href="#s7">7. Disclosure Requirements</a>
      <a href="#s8">8. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</a>
      <a href="#s9">9. Relationship to IAS/IFRS</a>
      <a href="#s10">10. Statement Mapping</a>
      <a href="#s11">11. Related Standards</a>
      <a href="#s12">12. Glossary</a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s1">
      <span class="num">1</span>
      <h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Refining deferred tax mechanics for interim reporting purposes</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 40 is the SECOND stage ("Part 2") of PARTIAL amendments to Japan's TAX EFFECT ACCOUNTING standard (ASBJ Statement No. 28 — see the companion poster), issued as PART of the SAME coordinated October 2025 package that PRODUCED ASBJ Statement No. 37 (Interim Financial Reporting). Given this COORDINATION, this amendment PLAUSIBLY addresses HOW deferred tax should be estimated and applied SPECIFICALLY within the CONDENSED, time-pressured context of INTERIM reporting.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2">
      <span class="num">2</span>
      <h2>Scope — Interim-Period Deferred Tax Mechanics</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Companies preparing interim financial statements with tax effect accounting implications</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to companies APPLYING tax effect accounting (deferred tax, per ASBJ Statement No. 28) WITHIN the context of PREPARING interim financial statements under ASBJ Statement No. 37 — addressing PRACTICAL questions that arise when a FULL, year-end-style deferred tax analysis is NOT practicable within the SHORTER, condensed interim reporting timeframe.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3">
      <span class="num">3</span>
      <h2>Why "Part 2" — Continuing the Tax Effect Accounting Reform Sequence</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">A recurring ASBJ pattern of incremental, sequential amendment</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">CONSISTENT with the SAME broader ASBJ PATTERN of incremental, staged standard refinement (ALSO seen in the retirement benefits reform and the "Part 3" cash flow statement amendments — ASBJ Statement No. 39), this "Part 2" designation REFLECTS a CONTINUING sequence of amendments to the UNDERLYING tax effect accounting standard, RATHER than a single, comprehensive rewrite.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4">
      <span class="num">4</span>
      <h2>Estimating an Effective Tax Rate for Interim Periods</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">A practical simplification for interim-period tax provisions</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">A COMMON approach for INTERIM-period income tax accounting — used INTERNATIONALLY under IAS 34 and broadly PARALLELED in J-GAAP practice — involves ESTIMATING an ANNUAL EFFECTIVE tax rate (based on FULL-YEAR projected results) and APPLYING that estimated rate to the INTERIM period's own pre-tax profit, RATHER than performing a FULL, discrete deferred tax computation for the SHORTER interim period ALONE. This Statement's amendments PLAUSIBLY refine or CLARIFY this practical approach, GIVEN its coordination with the BROADER interim reporting reform.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5">
      <span class="num">5</span>
      <h2>Coordination With the Interim Reporting Reform Package</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">A companion piece within the broader reform package</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">This Statement was issued ON THE SAME DATE as ASBJ Statement No. 37 (Interim Financial Reporting), No. 38 (consolidated interim preparation), and No. 39 (consolidated cash flow statement amendments) — CONFIRMING that TAX EFFECT accounting for INTERIM purposes was a SPECIFIC, deliberate focus of this COORDINATED reform effort.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6">
      <span class="num">6</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — Applying an Estimated Annual Effective Tax Rate at Interim</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">A practical simplification for the condensed interim period</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: Estimating interim tax expense using a projected annual rate</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A company estimates its FULL-YEAR effective tax rate at 32%, based on projected annual results. Interim (half-year) pre-tax profit is ¥400,000,000.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The company recognises INTERIM tax expense of ¥400,000,000 × 32% = <strong>¥128,000,000</strong> — APPLYING the ESTIMATED annual effective rate to the interim period's OWN pre-tax profit, a PRACTICAL simplification AVOIDING the need for a FULL, discrete deferred tax computation WITHIN the condensed interim reporting timeframe.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7">
      <span class="num">7</span>
      <h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 40 addresses</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Basis for the estimated annual effective tax rate applied at the interim reporting date</span>
          <span>Significant changes in the estimated effective tax rate since the last annual report</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8">
      <span class="num">8</span>
      <h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Whether the estimated annual effective tax rate approach is appropriate given the company's specific circumstances</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Projected full-year taxable income and effective tax rate</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9">
      <span class="num">9</span>
      <h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IAS 34's Interim Tax Approach</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">IAS 34 EXPLICITLY REQUIRES the estimated ANNUAL effective tax rate approach for interim tax provisions internationally — this Statement's LIKELY refinement of the SAME practical approach for J-GAAP purposes would represent a GENUINELY CONVERGED treatment, CONSISTENT with how J-GAAP's general interim reporting principles have ALREADY been broadly ALIGNED with IAS 34 (see the companion ASBJ Statement No. 37 poster).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10">
      <span class="num">10</span>
      <h2>Statement Mapping</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every interim tax event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Event</span>
            <span>Statement(s) affected</span>
            <span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Interim tax expense</span>
            <span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span>
            <span>Based on the estimated annual effective tax rate</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11">
      <span class="num">11</span>
      <h2>Related Standards</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2">
            <span>Standard</span>
            <span>Connection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 28</span>
            <span>Tax Effect Accounting — the underlying base standard this Statement partially amends</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 37</span>
            <span>The general interim reporting framework issued as part of the same coordinated reform package</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12">
      <span class="num">12</span>
      <h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Estimated annual effective tax rate</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">A projected full-year effective tax rate applied to interim-period pre-tax profit as a practical simplification, avoiding a full discrete deferred tax computation each interim period.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
      <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
      <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
      <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
      <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
    </div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
